{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>One day.</b> According to the word-order of the passage it should have written 'a first day,' as it writes for all the other days — second, third, fourth. Why did it write 'one'? Because the Holy One, blessed be He, was alone in His world — the angels had not yet been created until the second day. Thus it is expounded in Bereshit Rabbah."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:02.653587058Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}